WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.335
-Good to see you, buddy.
-Great to see you, as always.

00:00:03.335 --> 00:00:04.537
-Dude, congrats.
-Hey.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.639
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.240
-They love you.
They love you.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.709
We love you.
-I love you.

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.911
-I got a lot too --
I love me too.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.012
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:14.113
I want to get to the song.

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:15.248
-Yeah.
-But what a year you've had.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.150
First of all,
can I just recap for you?

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.684
-Sure.
-This is what happened to you.

00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:21.888
You were in "Jumanji"
and "Jumanji" made

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:24.257
almost $1 billion worldwide.
I don't know if you knew that.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.491
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:26.926
Biggest movie.
Congratulations.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.327
You were fantastic in it.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:30.863
-Then you got nominated for a
Golden Globe for your song

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:32.899
in "Ferdinand."

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:36.135
And then even the best news, the
biggest news, the coolest news.

00:00:36.135 --> 00:00:38.204
You got engaged to our buddy.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.272
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.873
Priyanka Chopra.

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:43.776
♪♪

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:46.679
I've got to say, dude,
she is the most fun person.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.514
We love her so much.
Priyanka Chopra.

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:50.182
-She's the best.
-How did you --

00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:54.086
how did you meet?
-Well, we met through a friend.

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:56.389
So we got connected first
over text

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.724
and we started talking
for a while,

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:00.760
and it was about six months
before we met up in person.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.096
And then we actually attended
the Met Gala

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.630
a few years ago together.
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.065
-Had a great time,
but it just --

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.466
-As friends.
-Just friends.

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:09.001
And our lives were kind of
taking us to different places.

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:11.370
And the thing that was funny,
is people would ask us,

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.373
both in an interview setting
and in private,

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.807
"Are you guys seeing
each other?"

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.308
And the answer was "No"
and people thought

00:01:16.308 --> 00:01:18.244
we were being coy.
And so did we --

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.012
until we cut to now
we're engaged

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:21.914
so the story sort of
wrote itself.

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:23.015
-Yeah, like, oops. Yeah.

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:24.216
-But you know, we then met up

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:25.718
a couple months ago --

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.353
I think five months ago now,

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.022
and it was kind of immediate

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:31.590
and I think we just knew it
was right and jumped right in

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.726
and we're very happy.
-Oh, that's fantastic, dude.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.294
I love that. I love her --

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:37.863
Please give her --
give her my best.

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:39.966
She's one of our favorites.
-She's here.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.066
-Is she here?
-She's here right now.

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:42.168
-Is she in the crowd?

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:44.671
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.639
-She's over there.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.008
-Ah! Hey, pal.
Hey, how are you?

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.143
Hi, hi, hi.
Oh. All right.

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:53.613
I mean -- I think.
I mean, I think she's okay.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.448
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:59.853
Oops. Sorry.
You know I love you, pal.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.921
Explain what this is about.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:06.258
So, we -- Okay, so after we got
engaged, we then went to India,

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:09.695
to her home country
and to Mumbai.

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:10.864
And my parents came along

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:12.798
and we did this beautiful
Roka ceremony.

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:14.934
-What is that?
-Basically, it's a confirmation

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.402
from both sides of the family

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.805
that they approve
of the engagement.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.873
And then there's some
beautiful prayers

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:24.276
and a connection just for the
family to have a chance to meet

00:02:24.276 --> 00:02:26.646
and hang out and get
to know each other.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.715
It's really incredible,
and you know,

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:32.085
we both left that ceremony
so full of joy.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.086
-How did your family
handle that?

00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:36.455
-They loved it.
My parents were blown away by

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:38.358
the love shared among
all the people.

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.491
And just the --
-a little different

00:02:39.491 --> 00:02:40.993
than New Jersey.
-A little different than Jersey.

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:42.228
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.896
But it was really special and
for she and I,

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.064
I think it was just nice to be
able to have that time

00:02:46.064 --> 00:02:47.700
with the family first.
And have that private moment.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.401
And be able to share with
the world afterwards.

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:52.505
But it's funny that we had
this beautiful ceremony,

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:55.040
and we felt so connected,
and our families all met.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.975
And it was spiritual.
And then we put it on Instagram.

00:02:56.975 --> 00:02:59.312
And we were like, "Oh, my God,
it's official."

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.314
-Now we Instagram.
Now it's real.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.416
Now they really have to do it.
Yeah.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.351
Do you guys --
there's a nice picture

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.587
of the family there on
Instagram.

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:12.391
Now uh, NP -- is that your logo?
Is that a logo for your --

00:03:12.391 --> 00:03:14.594
Do you guys have a celebrity
nickname?

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:17.096
-We --
-Priyanka, you can answer that.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.298
Do you have a celebrity
nickname?

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:21.433
-She likes Prick.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.433 --> 00:03:24.036
-No, no, no. Absolute no.
-I don't like that one.

00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:25.604
-Absolutely no.

00:03:25.604 --> 00:03:27.973
[ Laughs ]

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:29.441
I have to ask you this question

00:03:29.441 --> 00:03:30.910
because it's one of
my favorite stories.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:31.944
We were talking earlier today.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:33.045
Thanks for doing the bit,
by the way.

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:34.447
-Oh, it was great.
I had a lot of fun.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:35.481
-Love hanging out with you.

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.149
But you told me the story about

00:03:37.149 --> 00:03:39.051
going to the Golden Globes

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:40.552
and it must have been exciting.

00:03:40.552 --> 00:03:41.754
-Oh, gosh.
-I was like, "Was it exciting

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.422
for you?" And you go,
"yeah, I lost, but --"

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:44.957
just tell the story
'cause it's great.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:46.358
-Well, I feel like every time
I come here

00:03:46.358 --> 00:03:47.794
I tell you a really
embarrassing story by the way.

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.128
-Exactly.
And that's why --

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.897
And I love that you keep
coming back

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:52.332
and I keep making you
embarrass yourself.

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:54.366
-But it's sad that the first
thought I had

00:03:54.366 --> 00:03:55.767
when something embarrassing
happens is,

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:56.803
"I got to talk to Jimmy."

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:57.903
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.903 --> 00:03:59.305
-Please, always do that.
Please.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.542
-So, I'm at the Golden Globes.
I was very excited.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.543
I was so honored to be nominated
for the song.

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:06.979
And it was a real career
milestone for me.

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:08.313
-Yeah.
-And I'm sitting in the audience

00:04:08.313 --> 00:04:09.581
with my brother
who came with me.

00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:11.517
And they announced
the award and we lost.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.118
Or, I lost.
Me and my co-writers.

00:04:13.118 --> 00:04:14.487
And I was devastated.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:16.622
I was really hoping it would
happen and he said,

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:18.424
"Let's go to the bar,
let's grab a drink.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.259
Blow off some steam for a minute
and we'll go back inside."

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:21.260
-Yeah.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.962
-And so I go to
the bar with Joe.

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.664
I grab myself a beer,
and he gets one.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.632
And I'm hanging out and I've
heard all this talk that

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:28.467
Michael Keaton is arriving soon.

00:04:28.467 --> 00:04:29.935
People are whispering, "Michael
Keaton's coming over.

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:31.904
He's gonna come over."
And I'm thinking to myself,

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.639
"Wow, this is great. I'm so
excited to meet Michael Keaton."

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:35.675
-Yeah, I love Michael Keaton.
-And I've got my beer here

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:37.543
and there's a woman here trying
to take a picture of me and Joe.

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:39.412
And she bumps into us
as he approaches.

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:41.280
And the beer spills all over
Michael Keaton

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.882
just before he goes on stage
to present an award.

00:04:43.882 --> 00:04:46.419
So cut to three
or four days ago,

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.821
we're at the U.S. Open.
-This is the best.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:51.357
-And I kid you not.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:54.092
I walk in, shuffling to our
thing with the beer,

00:04:54.092 --> 00:04:55.227
and I see Michael Keaton.

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:56.896
It's like he locks eyes with me.
He's like --

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:57.897
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:59.599
"I hope you're not
drinking a beer."

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:01.767
-Yeah, you better
watch it Jonas."

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.035
-And I sat down.
-Yeah.

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:04.870
-I had the little bag on my
lap.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:07.873
Put my beer on the ground,
and he's right here.

00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:09.942
And the bag falls off
in slow motion.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.377
[ Audience oohs ]

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:12.511
Hits the beer.

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:14.113
And it spills below his feet.

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.848
[Laughter]

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:18.451
-All over --
All over Michael Keaton.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.952
-But it didn't hit him.

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:22.121
It was all over his feet
and I'm wondering now

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:24.457
if he knows that it was me
and he just ignored it.

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:26.692
Or if he was so mad that he just
let it go. I don't know.

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:27.926
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.926 --> 00:05:30.462
But it's a theme --
-But it's a theme for you.

00:05:30.462 --> 00:05:33.265
And that sounds like something
that would happen to me.

00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:35.234
-It's just so embarrassing
and of all people,

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.768
it's Michael Keaton.
-He's the greatest.

00:05:36.768 --> 00:05:38.004
-He's the coolest.
-Yeah.

00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:40.773
He's a good sport too.
Congrats on "Right Now."

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:41.841
-Thank you.
-I'm excited about this.

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:44.276
And you'll be performing
for us tonight.

00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:46.512
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:48.481
Not only are you writing
and performing songs,

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:50.649
but you're also writing
and performing --

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:52.285
writing movies and plays.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:53.352
Is that true?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:55.254
So I started writing,
actually --

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.789
another connection we have,

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:58.557
is that one of the times
I came before,

00:05:58.557 --> 00:05:59.859
we were talking about
gangster movies.

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.160
And I'm from Jersey and I hadn't
seen a lot

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.795
of these classic
Mafia movies.

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:04.497
-Oh, that was awful.
-So you were kind enough

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:06.132
to get me a gift basket
of all the movies.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:07.766
And I watched them all.
Most of them.

00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:09.234
-You did?
-"Sopranos."

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:10.970
-And I got so inspired

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.538
and it's close to home because
it's Jersey,

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:13.839
that I actually wrote a play

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:15.908
about the son of a wise guy in
Brooklyn, New York,

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:17.743
named Gino Castaluccio,

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:20.346
and we're doing our second
reading of the play next week.

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:22.181
-No way.
-Yeah. And so that --

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:24.050
and a couple films.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.651
-Dude, I love that.
-Thank you.

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.186
-I feel like
I inspired you.

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:30.189
-So I'm going to give you 50%
once we go on Broadway.

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:31.457
-No, no, no.
-It's only right.

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.092
-I just want a ticket to the
show. That's all I need.

